<!--
    Chart/summary metadata for the FitContributor fields created in
    ActivityController.mc (session.createField() ids must match these).
    Without this, sideloaded builds still write the fields into the FIT
    file correctly (confirmed via FitCSVTool), but tools that visualize
    FitContributor data, such as MonkeyGraph and Garmin Connect once/if
    this app is published to the store, have no chart/label config to
    render them with.

    hr_zone_seconds (id 0) is a 5 element array (seconds per HR zone for
    the whole session), so displayInChart is a reasonable fit, since it's
    inherently a small multi value breakdown, not a single scalar.
    skate_seconds/other_seconds (ids 1/2) are each a single cumulative
    total for the whole session, not a per second time series, so
    displayInActivitySummary (a plain summary stat) fits them better than
    displayInChart, which implies plotting a value over time and doesn't
    apply here since there's only one final value per session.

    lap_skate_distance (id 3) is MESG_TYPE_LAP in code, reset every lap,
    so displayInActivityLaps shows it as a per-lap breakdown rather than
    one session total.

    skate_speed/walk_speed (ids 4/5) are MESG_TYPE_RECORD (written every
    second), each nonzero only in its own state and zero otherwise. Both
    charted, in different colors, as an approximation of a single
    color-coded speed graph, since Garmin Connect's built-in Speed chart
    has no customization hook for third-party developer fields, so this
    is a separate pair of charts rather than a literal recoloring of
    that one.
    Whether these actually render overlaid into one visual line (the
    intent) or as two stacked charts is unconfirmed until tested.
-->
<resources xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://developer.garmin.com/downloads/connect-iq/resources.xsd">
    <fitContributions>
        <fitField id="0"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="0"
            precision="0"
            chartTitle="@Strings.HrZoneSecondsLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.HrZoneSecondsLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SecondsUnit"
            fillColor="#FF8800" />
        <fitField id="1"
            displayInActivitySummary="true"
            sortOrder="1"
            precision="0"
            dataLabel="@Strings.SkateSecondsLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SecondsUnit" />
        <fitField id="2"
            displayInActivitySummary="true"
            sortOrder="2"
            precision="0"
            dataLabel="@Strings.OtherSecondsLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SecondsUnit" />
        <fitField id="3"
            displayInActivityLaps="true"
            sortOrder="3"
            precision="0"
            dataLabel="@Strings.LapSkateDistanceLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.MetersUnit" />
        <fitField id="4"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="4"
            precision="1"
            chartTitle="@Strings.SkateSpeedLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.SkateSpeedLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SpeedUnit"
            fillColor="#00CC00" />
        <fitField id="5"
            displayInChart="true"
            sortOrder="5"
            precision="1"
            chartTitle="@Strings.WalkSpeedLabel"
            dataLabel="@Strings.WalkSpeedLabel"
            unitLabel="@Strings.SpeedUnit"
            fillColor="#888888" />
    </fitContributions>
</resources>
